Ladybird matches the letters typed into a select against its option
labels. Repeating a letter cycles through matches, and extending a
prefix starts at the current option. In a popup, typing highlights
the match and pressing Enter accepts it.

Blink calls TypeAhead::HandleEvent from HTMLSelectElement::
TypeAheadFind. WebKit calls TypeAhead::handleEvent with MatchPrefix
and CycleFirstChar. In Gecko, HTMLSelectElement::HandleKeyPress builds
the search string. IsOptionInteractivelySelectable filters the matches.

Chrome 158.0.8127.38, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 selected Finnish
on both fi and ff in a list containing a disabled Fiction option,
followed by French and Finnish. Each also selected Finnish when a
keydown listener replaced the options before the default action ran.

For list boxes, Ladybird skips options without a rendered row. Firefox
also skipped hidden and display:none options. Chrome and WebKit chose
those options when their labels matched. All three skipped disabled
options in both collapsed selects and list boxes.
